  "Nodes": [
    {
      "ConcreteType": "PythonNodeModels.PythonNode, PythonNodeModels",
      "Code": "\"\"\"\r\nDynamo Python3 (PythonNet3 engine) — Revit 2026\r\nFilter hanger family instances down to \"real\" (rod) hangers, excluding\r\nside-wall hangers, based on FAMILY NAME keyword matching.\r\n\r\nUse this as a step BEFORE the align_hanger_rods_to_structure.py script —\r\nwire its OUT into IN[0] of that script.\r\n\r\nINPUTS (IN):\r\n  IN[0] : list  - All candidate hanger family instances, from ALL your hanger\r\n                  families combined (e.g. multiple \"All Elements of Family Type\"\r\n                  nodes fed into a List.Join / List.Flatten before this node).\r\n  IN[1] : list of str (optional) - Keywords that, if found in the family name\r\n                  (case-insensitive), mean EXCLUDE this element.\r\n                  Defaults to [\"side wall\", \"sidewall\", \"wall hanger\"].\r\n  IN[2] : list of str (optional) - Keywords that, if provided, mean the family\r\n                  name must contain AT LEAST ONE of these to be INCLUDED\r\n                  (case-insensitive). Leave empty/unwired to skip this check\r\n                  (i.e. include everything not excluded by IN[1]).\r\n                  Example: [\"hanger\", \"rod\"] if all your rod-hanger families\r\n                  have \"Hanger\" or \"Rod\" somewhere in the name.\r\n\r\nOUTPUT (OUT):\r\n  A dictionary: {\"filtered\": [...], \"excluded\": [...], \"report\": [...]}\r\n  \"filtered\" is what you wire into the alignment script.\r\n  \"excluded\" and \"report\" are so you can sanity-check what got dropped.\r\n\"\"\"\r\n\r\nimport clr\r\nclr.AddReference('RevitAPI')\r\nfrom Autodesk.Revit.DB import FamilyInstance\r\n\r\ncandidates = UnwrapElement(IN[0]) if not isinstance(IN[0], list) else UnwrapElement(IN[0])\r\nif not isinstance(candidates, list):\r\n    candidates = [candidates]\r\n\r\nexclude_keywords = [k.lower() for k in IN[1]] if len(IN) > 1 and IN[1] else [\"side wall\", \"sidewall\", \"wall hanger\"]\r\ninclude_keywords = [k.lower() for k in IN[2]] if len(IN) > 2 and IN[2] else []\r\n\r\nfiltered = []\r\nexcluded = []\r\nreport = []\r\n\r\nfor el in candidates:\r\n    try:\r\n        if isinstance(el, FamilyInstance):\r\n            fam_name = el.Symbol.Family.Name\r\n        else:\r\n            # Fallback for non-FamilyInstance elements (shouldn't normally hit this)\r\n            fam_name = el.Name\r\n\r\n        fam_name_lower = fam_name.lower()\r\n\r\n        is_excluded = any(kw in fam_name_lower for kw in exclude_keywords)\r\n        is_included = True if not include_keywords else any(kw in fam_name_lower for kw in include_keywords)\r\n\r\n        if is_excluded or not is_included:\r\n            excluded.append(el)\r\n            reason = \"matched exclude keyword\" if is_excluded else \"did not match include keyword\"\r\n            report.append(\"Element {} | Family '{}' | EXCLUDED ({})\".format(el.Id.Value, fam_name, reason))\r\n        else:\r\n            filtered.append(el)\r\n            report.append(\"Element {} | Family '{}' | INCLUDED\".format(el.Id.Value, fam_name))\r\n\r\n    except Exception as e:\r\n        excluded.append(el)\r\n        report.append(\"Element {}: ERROR reading family name - {}\".format(el.Id.Value, str(e)))\r\n\r\nOUT = {\r\n    \"filtered\": filtered,\r\n    \"excluded\": excluded,\r\n    \"counts\": {\"total\": len(candidates), \"filtered\": len(filtered), \"excluded\": len(excluded)},\r\n    \"report\": report\r\n}\r\n",
      "Engine": "CPython3",
      "VariableInputPorts": true,
      "Id": "ef1c992ce4b846938f64fc4d2cba53d9",
      "NodeType": "PythonScriptNode",
