    {
      "ConcreteType": "PythonNodeModels.PythonNode, PythonNodeModels",
      "Code": "\"\"\"\r\nDynamo Python3 (PythonNet3 engine) — Revit 2026\r\nCollect elements of a given category that are visible/present within a\r\nSPECIFIC view only (respects that view's crop box, visibility/graphics\r\noverrides, and phase) — instead of collecting from the whole model.\r\n\r\nUse this in place of the \"Categories + All Elements of Category\" nodes at\r\nthe start of your graph. Its output feeds into the same filter script\r\n(filter_hangers_exclude_sidewall.py) exactly as before.\r\n\r\nINPUTS (IN):\r\n  IN[0] : View element OR string - Either wire in a Revit View element\r\n                 directly (e.g. from Dynamo's \"Views\" / \"Select Model Element\"\r\n                 node, or \"Views.GetByName\"), OR pass the exact view name as\r\n                 a string and this script will look it up for you.\r\n  IN[1] : str (optional) - Built-in category name to collect, as it appears\r\n                 after \"OST_\" in the Revit API (e.g. \"PipeAccessory\").\r\n                 Defaults to \"PipeAccessory\" to match your hanger setup.\r\n\r\nOUTPUT (OUT):\r\n  A dictionary: {\"elements\": [...], \"view_name\": \"...\", \"count\": N}\r\n  Wire OUT[\"elements\"] into the filter script's IN[0], same as before.\r\n\"\"\"\r\n\r\nimport clr\r\nclr.AddReference('RevitServices')\r\nclr.AddReference('RevitAPI')\r\n\r\nfrom RevitServices.Persistence import DocumentManager\r\nfrom Autodesk.Revit.DB import FilteredElementCollector, BuiltInCategory, View\r\n\r\ndoc = DocumentManager.Instance.CurrentDBDocument\r\n\r\nview_input = UnwrapElement(IN[0])\r\ncategory_name = IN[1] if len(IN) > 1 and IN[1] else \"PipeAccessory\"\r\n\r\n# Resolve the view: accept either an actual View element, or a name string.\r\ntarget_view = None\r\nif isinstance(view_input, View):\r\n    target_view = view_input\r\nelif isinstance(view_input, str):\r\n    all_views = FilteredElementCollector(doc).OfClass(View).WhereElementIsNotElementType().ToElements()\r\n    for v in all_views:\r\n        if not v.IsTemplate and v.Name == view_input:\r\n            target_view = v\r\n            break\r\n\r\nif target_view is None:\r\n    OUT = {\"error\": \"Could not resolve a view from IN[0]. Check the view name matches exactly, or wire in a View element directly.\", \"elements\": [], \"count\": 0}\r\nelse:\r\n    try:\r\n        bic = getattr(BuiltInCategory, \"OST_\" + category_name)\r\n    except AttributeError:\r\n        OUT = {\"error\": \"Unknown category name '{}'. Check the exact BuiltInCategory spelling.\".format(category_name), \"elements\": [], \"count\": 0}\r\n    else:\r\n        collector = FilteredElementCollector(doc, target_view.Id).OfCategory(bic).WhereElementIsNotElementType()\r\n        elements = list(collector.ToElements())\r\n\r\n        OUT = {\r\n            \"elements\": elements,\r\n            \"view_name\": target_view.Name,\r\n            \"count\": len(elements)\r\n        }",
      "Engine": "CPython3",
      "VariableInputPorts": true,
      "Id": "36e93da1a9574af4a64229e5cf956a2f",
      "NodeType": "PythonScriptNode",
      "Inputs": [
        {
          "Id": "d19c471bab80409dbd11c9338e4f1ac6",
          "Name": "IN[0]",
          "Description": "Input #0",
          "UsingDefaultValue": false,
          "Level": 2,
          "UseLevels": false,
          "KeepListStructure": false
        },
        {
          "Id": "9ef6147570e84b499687d2e6bfa4c0aa",
          "Name": "IN[1]",
          "Description": "Input #1",
          "UsingDefaultValue": false,
          "Level": 2,
